# A dict view prints as a VIEW, not as a list (roadmap Gap R.182, owner L11.1; ADR 0296)
#
# Three bugs on one row. Before this change:
#   print({"a": 1}.keys())      reference dict_keys(['a'])    --interp ['a']    --aot 0
#   print({1: 2}.values())      reference dict_values([2])    --interp [2]      --aot EXIT 2
# The compiled fold rendered a folded literal as the ADDRESS of a compile-time global and handed it to
# a heap walker -- rt_print_list_mixed(i32 @.lst1, i32 0) -- which is exit 2, ADR 0166's own-bug code.
# And neither engine said the wrapper word that tells a view apart from a list.
#
# A view stays a list-SHAPED object (sum/min/max/len/for/in all keep working on it); only its
# rendering knows it is a view. items() stays a refusal on the compiled leg until L11.3 gives a pair
# a value to be, which is why it is not in this file.
print({"a": 1}.keys())
print({"a": 1, "b": 2}.keys())
print({"a": 1}.values())
print({1: 2}.values())
print({1: "a"}.values())
print({}.keys())
print({}.values())
print(sum({1: 2, 3: 4}.keys()))
print(max({1: 2, 3: 4}.keys()))
print(min({1: 2, 3: 4}.keys()))
print([1, 2])
print({"a": 1})
